  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-1",
      "transcript": "Why can their fingers make you laugh, but yours usually can't?",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 3.825,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.45a8e4181c1b1913e125d41dfe1da790f71d370a7bc6c2b22f773ef8756681e1",
        "sha256": "45a8e4181c1b1913e125d41dfe1da790f71d370a7bc6c2b22f773ef8756681e1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-2",
      "transcript": "Both touch your skin. One important clue is prediction.",
      "start": 4,
      "duration": 3.625,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.5004b88f1178f6666fa379be403cbe8223526c0dcb1dd2b02b42795d97994df5",
        "sha256": "5004b88f1178f6666fa379be403cbe8223526c0dcb1dd2b02b42795d97994df5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-3",
      "transcript": "When you move your hand, your nervous system can anticipate the touch it will produce.",
      "start": 7.8,
      "duration": 4.975,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.9208e35c877ec451626b395ca5121afc29aca2d0e5eeb4522081e7d0c7059e10",
        "sha256": "9208e35c877ec451626b395ca5121afc29aca2d0e5eeb4522081e7d0c7059e10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-4",
      "transcript": "That touch can feel weaker. Scientists call this sensory attenuation.",
      "start": 13,
      "duration": 4.775,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.0b442a8554c24411b1b6319b75b78174bdc063be8725c804e2500e36417bfb5b",
        "sha256": "0b442a8554c24411b1b6319b75b78174bdc063be8725c804e2500e36417bfb5b"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-5",
      "transcript": "In experiments, self-produced touch felt less ticklish than matching external touch.",
      "start": 18.033333333333335,
      "duration": 5.275,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.2a162e2192416f8514942d6d2606a1a552f5ff87532312e924b33ecf2e14e317",
        "sha256": "2a162e2192416f8514942d6d2606a1a552f5ff87532312e924b33ecf2e14e317"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-6",
      "transcript": "Adding a delay to a robotic self-touch made it feel more ticklish.",
      "start": 23.533333333333335,
      "duration": 4.3,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.aa1a08cc75e37609a8027aae2a394ac8e183729093967c6a359dc5f58574d919",
        "sha256": "aa1a08cc75e37609a8027aae2a394ac8e183729093967c6a359dc5f58574d919"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-7",
      "transcript": "But those experiments used light touch, not full-on tickle laughter.",
      "start": 28.033333333333335,
      "duration": 4.35,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.15e1c0241bb0e7c9fec6042c7d0fe8ff56456ae5d5f9d590aacbd9cf553d86f5",
        "sha256": "15e1c0241bb0e7c9fec6042c7d0fe8ff56456ae5d5f9d590aacbd9cf553d86f5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-8",
      "transcript": "You can give yourself a light, tickly sensation. Laughter-inducing tickling is harder to explain, and people differ.",
      "start": 32.56666666666667,
      "duration": 7.4,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.b04a113d0a59ccc848773fb96e79657754099fdd5d655722752627ab62b1e8c4",
        "sha256": "b04a113d0a59ccc848773fb96e79657754099fdd5d655722752627ab62b1e8c4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-9",
      "transcript": "Prediction is an important clue, not the whole answer.",
      "start": 40.166666666666664,
      "duration": 3.575,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.d6ea075ebe9995abca830817e738507d5a3c2c64996368178df56e7738ac186d",
        "sha256": "d6ea075ebe9995abca830817e738507d5a3c2c64996368178df56e7738ac186d"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "self-tickle-cue-10",
      "transcript": "Your nervous system doesn't just receive touch. It can anticipate your own.",
      "start": 44.03333333333333,
      "duration": 4.625,
      "media": {
        "id": "media.b6401b6b30d0b417fccecae6a3cdcff2240bedc3e96f3f6d03a360b78a6c8104",
        "sha256": "b6401b6b30d0b417fccecae6a3cdcff2240bedc3e96f3f6d03a360b78a6c8104"
      }
    }
  ],
